    difficulty: "beginner",
    duration: 60,
    technologies: ["Bolt.new"],
    learningOutcomes: ["Going from idea to a live public web page now takes under an hour and costs nothing"],
    prerequisites: null,
    content: "# Ship It: Publish a Real Web Page to the Internet\n\n> **Stage:** idea awaiting full write-up. The detail below is the approved lab idea (June 2026 free-tier facts checked 12 June 2026). Full lab.md, voiceover and image prompts follow once this idea is picked.\n\n- **Type:** Build\n- **Lesson(s):** L16 (AI Presentations and Websites), L09 (Building)\n- **Tools and access:** Bolt.new free (300K tokens/day and free hosting with a shareable URL, confirmed on bolt.new/pricing 12 June 2026). Browser only, no card.\n- **The task:** Students build and publish a genuine one-page site for something real in their life: a CV landing page, a club or community group page, or a family event page. Flow: one descriptive prompt, two improvement rounds (\"make the headline section calmer\", \"add a contact section\"), then press publish and open the live URL on their phone to prove it is really on the internet. The L04 data rule applies: no home address or phone number on a public page.\n- **Timing:** 5 min sign in to Bolt; 10 min plan content with any chatbot (\"interview me, then write the copy for my one-page site\"); 30 min build with two improvement rounds; 8 min publish and test the URL on a phone; 7 min save the URL and screenshots. Total 60.\n- **What the student learns:** Going from idea to a live public web page now takes under an hour and costs nothing.\n- **Deliverable:** A live URL they can send to anyone, plus a phone screenshot of it loading.\n- **Difficulty:** Mid M1.",
    instructions: [{ step: 1, title: "Lab Walkthrough", content: "# Ship It: Publish a Real Web Page to the Internet\n\n> **Stage:** idea awaiting full write-up. The detail below is the approved lab idea (June 2026 free-tier facts checked 12 June 2026). Full lab.md, voiceover and image prompts follow once this idea is picked.\n\n- **Type:** Build\n- **Lesson(s):** L16 (AI Presentations and Websites), L09 (Building)\n- **Tools and access:** Bolt.new free (300K tokens/day and free hosting with a shareable URL, confirmed on bolt.new/pricing 12 June 2026). Browser only, no card.\n- **The task:** Students build and publish a genuine one-page site for something real in their life: a CV landing page, a club or community group page, or a family event page. Flow: one descriptive prompt, two improvement rounds (\"make the headline section calmer\", \"add a contact section\"), then press publish and open the live URL on their phone to prove it is really on the internet. The L04 data rule applies: no home address or phone number on a public page.\n- **Timing:** 5 min sign in to Bolt; 10 min plan content with any chatbot (\"interview me, then write the copy for my one-page site\"); 30 min build with two improvement rounds; 8 min publish and test the URL on a phone; 7 min save the URL and screenshots. Total 60.\n- **What the student learns:** Going from idea to a live public web page now takes under an hour and costs nothing.\n- **Deliverable:** A live URL they can send to anyone, plus a phone screenshot of it loading.\n- **Difficulty:** Mid M1." }],
