    content: "# Your Month 1 Portfolio Page\n\n> **Stage:** idea awaiting full write-up. The detail below is the approved lab idea (June 2026 free-tier facts checked 12 June 2026). Full lab.md, voiceover and image prompts follow once this idea is picked.\n\n- **Type:** Build\n- **Lesson(s):** L25 (Month 1 Portfolio)\n- **Tools and access:** Bolt.new free (hosting included) or Claude Artifacts (free) for students who prefer not to publish publicly. Plus the saved outputs of every previous lab.\n- **The task:** Students assemble their best 5 lab deliverables (the live site URL from Lab 17, the dashboard, the poster, a scoring sheet that changed their mind, the FamilyBot brief) into a single \"What I can do with AI\" page. They use any chatbot to interview them first (\"ask me five questions about what I am proudest of from this month, then write the copy\"), then build the page with one prompt and two refinement rounds. Public publishing is optional; a screenshot suffices for the GWTH Score evidence.\n- **Timing:** 10 min gather the 5 artefacts; 10 min interview and copywriting with a chatbot; 25 min build the page with two refinement rounds; 10 min final read-through against the honesty rule (claim only what they did); 5 min save URL or screenshot. Total 60.\n- **What the student learns:** A month of small labs adds up to demonstrable, showable capability, which is the whole point of the GWTH Score.\n- **Deliverable:** A portfolio page (live URL or screenshot) presenting 5 artefacts from the month.\n- **Difficulty:** Late M1.",
